Subject: Modeling Algorithms - BRepGProp_Gauss refines U to the requested precision, as it refines L
Upstream: https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/issues/1675 (BRepGProp_Gauss never refines U; a PR needs OCCT's CLA)
Applies to: OCCT V7_9_3, after 0003 (which changes BRepGProp_Face.cxx only; this patch is
     against the pinned BRepGProp_Gauss.hxx and BRepGProp_Gauss.cxx).
Why: BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute with an Eps (BRepGProp::VolumeProperties and SurfaceProperties
     with an eps, Silico's precise measure) never refines U: EpsU starts at 0 and is set only
     in a branch the U loop can't reach, so the loop ends after its first pass, and U is
     integrated once, at SIntOrder(eps) points on each span UKnots gives. U's error is also
     left out of the estimate (ErrUL is set only on the first L order's pass). So an
     extruded two-span B-spline measured 9.4e-4 low and its swept face's area 0.27% high,
     a slanted prism of a one-span B-spline (the stress test's) 5.2% low in area, B-spline
     surfaces' areas up to about 1e-5 off, and one NIST part's volume 3.6e-5 off, each
     with an estimate of about 1e-16. This patch computes U's error on both L orders'
     passes, refreshes it on every U pass, and sets EpsU once, at the end of the first
     pass, as EpsL is, so U subdivides until it meets eps or the subdivision cap, whose
     branch (EpsU = ErrorU, break) ends it. Setting EpsU alone isn't enough: U would refine
     on the first L order's pass only, and the two L orders would disagree by U's error.
     U's tolerance is the requested precision of each strip's magnitude, 0.9 * eps * M,
     where M is the first pass's integral of the absolute values of the volume element's
     terms (|x xn| + |y yn| + |z zn|) / 3, and for areas the strip itself (its terms are
     w |n|, never negative). M is the strip's value wherever its terms don't cancel; where
     they do (a face whose plane holds the point the volume is integrated about, the mean
     of the shape's vertices) the strip's value is round-off and no scale, and a tolerance
     relative to it took U to its cap at every L point (a 60x60-span planar B-spline face
     0.25 s -> 59 s). A face whose initial spans already reach the subdivision cap (1953
     and more) gets no U tolerance and is integrated as before, bit for bit, where a
     refinement past the cap ran off OCCT's arrays; and none where the computation isn't
     verified (a negative Eps: estimate, don't refine), as L's loop has it. U's interval to
     split, and its error, are the largest of the current strip's intervals only: the error
     vector is cleared to each strip's own cap, so a search of the whole vector found a
     wider earlier strip's stale errors past it and split intervals the strip doesn't have
     (a triangle-trimmed rough B-spline face measured worse than unpatched, and a trimmed
     1000-span one took past 60 s, where it takes 1 s unpatched and about 5 s with this
     patch). The magnitude reaches
     computeVInertiaOfElementaryPart through a pointer defaulting to NULL, so the default
     integration (Compute without an Eps, FreeCAD's), a different function, is unchanged
     to the bit.
Moves: tests/determinism/oracle-reference.json's summary hashes of 113 of its 208 cases (151
     with Silico's measure about the shape's box centre, bridge.cpp, which moves 100; the
     list is the diff of that file in the commit that re-records it), to be re-recorded
     with the maintainer: volumes by at most 1.8e-13 relative, areas not at all, centres
     of mass by at most 4.6e-10 of the shape's size; not their measures, B-reps, meshes,
     histories, or topologies. No committed fingerprint (every golden and committed
     document checks and formats unchanged), and not the stress reference (default
     integration). Re-measured on this patch, with its search of only the strip's own
     intervals (2026-10-25).
Drop when: an OCCT release refines U in BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute's Eps path (check that
     EpsU is set by the end of the U loop's first pass, so the loop can go on), or when
     extruded_bsplines.rs passes with the patch removed; and only once
     adversarial_measure_refine_u.rs's tests in time and at the cap (its faces through the
     vertex mean, its rough faces of 1952, 1953, and 2000 spans, and its triangles) pass
     on that release too.

